Turns off the two rules this pin needs off together; its doc comment says
either one alone keeps it. A deny no longer waits while the folder is paused:
the Paused check at the top of the deny arm of FolderState::unsettled, added
by f6cff50 (Queue deny and revert until the folder settles), is removed. And
revert no longer returns the held item an unannounced deny consumed: it
forgets the denied items instead of calling Quarantine::return_denied, so the
item is dropped as deny's release dropped it before 0a9c82a (Return a held
item when revert discards the deny that consumed it). Both rules are DESIGN.md
§8.3's settled folder.

